#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""meta homelab: the homelab centre's module for the `meta` front door (brain record 0019).

One executable that describes itself (`--meta-manifest`) and answers four read-only verbs:

  status            Proxmox quorum and nodes, Kubernetes (Talos) nodes, Flux Kustomizations
                    and HelmReleases, Ceph health and usage, the newest backup per job
  list <what>       services | nodes | backups, one name per line, sorted
  show <service>    one service in detail, `key: value` lines (exit 5 if there is none)
  backlog           open issues and pull requests across the eight homelab repos

"Services" are the Deployments the Flux Kustomization `apps` manages (label
kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/name=apps), in every namespace.

Everything here reads. Python 3 standard library only. Sources, all read-only:
  kubectl get nodes | Flux Kustomizations and HelmReleases | CronJobs and Jobs labelled
  app.kubernetes.io/component=backup | Deployments of `apps` | Traefik IngressRoutes
  ssh pve-01 pvesh get /cluster/status | ssh pve-01 ceph status
  gh api graphql (issue and pull-request numbers and titles)

Environment from the core: META_JSON=1 (or --json), META_TIMEOUT (seconds left; each source
call stops before it). Exit codes are record 0019 §3's: 0 ok, 1 a problem found, 2 usage,
4 a live source unreachable, 5 not found, 6 this module broke.
"""

